    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (65.41) and **Tyler Freeman** (64.42), who represent our strongest offensive upside for today\u2019s slate. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive park-factor boost (+10%) and an advantageous matchup against the right-handed Jos\u00e9 Soriano, while **Tyler Freeman** thrives in his own hitter-friendly venue with an elite projection for volume. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.07) and **Taylor Ward** (63.85) provide high-floor stability; **Taylor Ward** is a particularly intriguing play today, as the combination of an leadoff spot (+10%) and favorable wind conditions (+5%) helps mitigate the tough matchup against Roki Sasaki, maintaining his daily efficiency well above our 60-point threshold.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Drew Gilbert**, whose 37.09 score ultimately relegated him to the bench. While his platoon advantage against Bachar provided a marginal lift, the combination of a low-value #8 batting position and a stiff SP skill discount pushed him firmly below our 40-point floor. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Gavin Sheets**, who squeaked into the starting lineup with a 41.13 despite facing the formidable Jacob deGrom. His selection is a testament to the scarcity of high-efficiency hitters today, though the risk of a sub-40 performance is acute given deGrom's dominance.\n\nSeveral risks loom over this lineup, most notably the prevalence of \"Lineup Pending\" tags. We are heavily reliant on the assumption that **Cal Raleigh** will slot into the #2 spot, which provides an 8% boost to his 59.84 score; should he shift down the order, that efficiency will dip significantly. Additionally, while we are managing the IL absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho**, the squad remains lean on elite stolen base threats. We need **Masyn Winn** and **Jeremiah Jackson** to be aggressive on the basepaths, as their matchups\u2014specifically **Jeremiah Jackson** facing Roki Sasaki\u2014necessitate high-leverage production to keep our Roto standing secure.",
